# --- uses: ["core"] injects core builtins into document scope
# B-347 investigation: inject_builtin_aliases is only called on builtins_env (the parent
# env for prelude type-checking), not on the user-facing env. The user-facing env is built
# by merge_env_bindings_into which copies only frames ABOVE builtins_env as baseline —
# so builtin-* aliases in the baseline frame do NOT leak into user scope. T002 should fire
# for raw builtin-* access without --- uses: ["core"]. The TODO(B-332) about disappeared
# warnings has not been reproduced; no regression from S-844 was found.
--- uses: ["core"]
[result: [builtin-if true "yes" "no"]]
=== out
Dict({"result": String("yes")})
